            <div xml:id="d886">

                <pb facs="0967" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/391: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-09-30T14:00:00-05:00">September 30,
                            1940—2 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2951. Following cable just received from Ankara [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Istanbul</hi>] (No. 107 of September 28):</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Please consult at once with British authorities as to best means of executing
                    this arrangement with the British Government.</p>
                <pb facs="0968" n="956" xml:id="pg956"/>
                <p>Advise upon quantities and grades that will be available (the Defense Commission
                    wants as much as it can get as soon as it can get it) and terms of payment. Also
                    please discuss shipping arrangements.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
